From b071edc1c93e95c49f65808d9e53abab50fe608c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HampterDev <131729366+HampterDev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 14:36:57 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Read monster skill actions without copying them into 8-byte
 buffers

session_get_monster_skill_info copied the text of the <action> and
<loopType> nodes of monsterskillinfo.xml into actionText[8] and
loopText[8] with sprintf, using the text as the format, and then parsed
them with atoi. A value of 8 or more characters overran the stack, and a
% in a value read arguments that were never passed. On the path for
players who are not administrators a missing <action> or <loopType>
node reached node_text(NULL), and xml_node_text dereferences its
argument.

The values are now parsed with atoi straight from the node text, and a
missing node counts as 0, the value the administrator path already
sets. The text is no longer passed through text_decode first: atoi
reads only blanks, a sign and digits, and the Korean-service mirror maps
each of those bytes to itself and no other byte to one of them, so
every result is the same as before.

The monster name, a job name from the client's Lua tables, is copied
into name[0x100] with a bound instead of strcpy; a longer name finds no
entry.

Validation: the new test_monster_skill_info runs the extracted function
over monsterskillinfo.xml parsed by core/xml.c, once with plain tags and
once with tags mirrored as for the Korean service: plain values, a
12-character value, a value with text after the number, "5%d%s%n",
"%n9", empty values, missing <action>, <loopType> or both, unknown
skills and monsters, a 767-byte monster name, and the administrator
path with its two message boxes. 32 lookups. The test fails on the
previous code, and with only the strcpy restored. Release build without
warnings.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VaQB81YtRGLtH8zvfX7WTY
